  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Acts",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "An angel ministers to Cornelius—Peter, in a vision, is commanded to take the gospel to the Gentiles—The gospel is taught by witnesses—The Holy Ghost falls upon the Gentiles.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "There was a certain man in Cæsarea called Cornelius, a centurion of the band called the Italian band,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:1",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "A devout man, and one that feared God with all his house, which gave much alms to the people, and prayed to God alway.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Almsgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Almsgiving.",
            "prettyString": "TG Almsgiving",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Almsgiving",
                "entryId": "tg-almsgiving",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:2",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "He saw in a vision evidently about the ninth hour of the day an angel of God coming in to him, and saying unto him, Cornelius.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Vision."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "GR clearly, distinctly."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "2 Ne. 32:3; Moro. 7:22 (22–38)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Vision.",
            "prettyString": "TG Vision",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Vision",
                "entryId": "tg-vision",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:3",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he looked on him, he was afraid, and said, What is it, Lord? And he said unto him, Thy prayers and thine alms are come up for a memorial before God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:4",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And now send men to Joppa, and call for one Simon, whose surname is Peter:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:5",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "He lodgeth with one Simon a tanner, whose house is by the sea side: he shall tell thee what thou oughtest to do.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:6",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And when the angel which spake unto Cornelius was departed, he called two of his household servants, and a devout soldier of them that waited on him continually;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:7",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he had declared all these things unto them, he sent them to Joppa.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:8",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "On the morrow, as they went on their journey, and drew nigh unto the city, Peter went up upon the housetop to pray about the sixth hour:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "1 Sam. 9:25 (25–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:9",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And he became very hungry, and would have eaten: but while they made ready, he fell into a trance,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "Acts 22:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Acts 22:17.",
            "prettyString": "Acts 22:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "acts",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 22,
                    "end": 22,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:10",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And saw heaven opened, and a certain vessel descending unto him, as it had been a great sheet knit at the four corners, and let down to the earth:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "D&C 107:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "GR bound."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 107:19.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 107:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 107,
                    "end": 107,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:11",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherein were all manner of fourfooted beasts of the earth, and wild beasts, and creeping things, and fowls of the air.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:12",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And there came a voice to him, Rise, Peter; kill, and eat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:13",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But Peter said, Not so, Lord; for I have never eaten any thing that is common or unclean.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Lev. 11:2 (2–47)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:14",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And the voice spake unto him again the second time, What God hath cleansed, that call not thou common.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Lev. 20:25. TG Cleanliness; Purification."
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 101,
            "text": "Acts 11:9; 1 Ne. 17:35 (32–41)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:15",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "This was done thrice: and the vessel was received up again into heaven.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:16",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Now while Peter doubted in himself what this vision which he had seen should mean, behold, the men which were sent from Cornelius had made inquiry for Simon’s house, and stood before the gate,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:17",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And called, and asked whether Simon, which was surnamed Peter, were lodged there.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:18",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "While Peter thought on the vision, the Spirit said unto him, Behold, three men seek thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Gifts of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Holy Ghost, Gifts of.",
            "prettyString": "TG Holy Ghost, Gifts of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Holy Ghost, Gifts of",
                "entryId": "tg-holy-ghost-gifts-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:19",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Arise therefore, and get thee down, and go with them, doubting nothing: for I have sent them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Acts 15:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Acts 15:7.",
            "prettyString": "Acts 15:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "acts",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 15,
                    "end": 15,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:20",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Peter went down to the men which were sent unto him from Cornelius; and said, Behold, I am he whom ye seek: what is the cause wherefore ye are come?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 120
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:21",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said, Cornelius the centurion, a just man, and one that feareth God, and of good report among all the nation of the Jews, was warned from God by an holy angel to send for thee into his house, and to hear words of thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "TG Warn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Warn.",
            "prettyString": "TG Warn",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Warn",
                "entryId": "tg-warn",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:22",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Then called he them in, and lodged them. And on the morrow Peter went away with them, and certain brethren from Joppa accompanied him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:23",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And the morrow after they entered into Cæsarea. And Cornelius waited for them, and had called together his kinsmen and near friends.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:24",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And as Peter was coming in, Cornelius met him, and fell down at his feet, and worshipped him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 10:25",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "But Peter took him up, saying, Stand up; I myself also am a man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Rev. 19:10; D&C 20:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Rev. 19:10; D&C 20:19.",
            "prettyString": "Revelation 19:10; D&C 20:19",
            "references": [
